Description: Install post_boot init scripts to /usr/libexec instead of /etc
 The post_boot scripts are vendor-provided executables that apply kernel and
 sysfs tuning at startup, not configuration an administrator is expected to
 edit, so per Debian Policy 9.1.1 they belong under /usr rather than /etc.
 Installing them below /etc also makes them conffiles, so dpkg prompts on
 upgrade whenever an upstream release changes their contents.
 .
 Move them to /usr/libexec/urm/initscripts/post_boot/ via
 CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBEXECDIR, and resolve the dispatcher's search directory from
 its own path instead of hardcoding /etc, so post_boot.sh keeps finding its
 target-specific siblings wherever the tree is installed.
 .
 The urm.service unit gained a matching ExecStartPre for the new location in
 userspace-resource-manager 0.4.3-0qli+staging2.
Author: Lukas Märdian <lukas.maerdian@oss.qualcomm.com>
Bug: https://github.com/qualcomm-linux/pkg-urm-ext/issues/23
Forwarded: https://github.com/qualcomm/userspace-resource-manager-extensions/pull/108
Last-Update: 2026-08-11
Index: pkg-urm-ext/CMakeLists.txt
===================================================================
--- pkg-urm-ext.orig/CMakeLists.txt
+++ pkg-urm-ext/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -32,10 +32,12 @@ install(
     DESTINATION ${CMAKE_INSTALL_SYSCONFDIR}/urm/target
 )
 
-# Install post_boot scripts to /etc/urm/initscripts/post_boot/
+# Install post_boot scripts to /usr/libexec/urm/initscripts/post_boot/
+# These are vendor-provided executables, not configuration, so they do not
+# belong below /etc.
 install(
     DIRECTORY ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/initscripts/post_boot/
-    DESTINATION ${CMAKE_INSTALL_SYSCONFDIR}/urm/initscripts/post_boot
+    DESTINATION ${CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBEXECDIR}/urm/initscripts/post_boot
     FILES_MATCHING
     PATTERN "*.sh"
     PERMISSIONS
